It runs the commands of the computers of the user's own TRIGGERcmd account
through the TRIGGERcmd API (https://docs.triggercmd.com), with the token of that
account. This integration is not affiliated with nor endorsed by TRIGGERcmd.
The endpoints follow the TRIGGERcmd documentation, the official agent
(https://github.com/rvmey/TRIGGERcmd-Agent, MIT), the official MCP server and
Mission Control client of TRIGGERcmd, and the answers of the live API to a
wrong token; the socket protocol of the "Gladys" computer follows the official
agent (Sails over socket.io 2). The Home Assistant "TRIGGERcmd" integration and
its "triggercmd" library were read for the on/off behaviour of the commands. No
code is taken from any of them.
